    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d668">

                <pb facs="0699" n="601" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg601"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">493.11/1527</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-08-08">August 8, 1930</date>.<lb/>[Received September
                        10.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 376</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to enclose a copy of a
                    despatch No. 968, of July 28, 1930,<anchor n="53" xml:id="d668-f1"/> entitled
                    “Claim Against Chinese Government for Property Destroyed by Rebel Army”, from
                    the Consul General at Canton.</p>
                <p>Likewise enclosed is a copy of my reply of to-day’s date in which the Legation
                    gives expression to the belief that the destruction of property by troops in
                    revolt against the central authorities constitutes a valid basis for a claim
                    filed with the latter.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Nelson Trusler
                    Johnson</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d668-a1.xml" xpointer="d668-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
